WEBVTT

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:03.990
Let me be clear.

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.560
I won't let you finish a thousand kilometers.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.360
He jumped ahead! He's got it!

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.450
You've gotten stronger. 
I hardly recognize you.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.120
But you're still...

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.950
Ordinary!

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:27.080
That's how strong you are.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.000
Feel like giving up yet?

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.360
Looks like there won't be any time for 
tea until I finish a thousand kilometers.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.160
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:12.000
<i>RIDE.14 The Ordinary Man and the Genius</i>

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:09.980
Teshima...

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:15.920
When you're unable to speak anymore, 
that'll be when you've given up.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.570
I'll become the captain 
of Sohoku High School.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:24.790
Teshima-san!

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.640
Who's becoming captain?

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.130
In any case, if we're celebrating, 
I'll have to order...

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.130
One of your favorite pizzas.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.460
Keep up, Teshima!

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.150
What? Damn it!

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.940
Are your legs cramping up?

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.360
Disappointing.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:01.360
That's your limit as an ordinary man!

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:08.660
An ordinary man can't lead 
men overflowing with talent.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:15.140
There was a bug on my leg,
so I shooed it away.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.090
Anyway, sorry, Koga.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:21.720
I believe there are things only 
an ordinary man like me can do!

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:24.760
I...

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.440
...don't think so.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.690
That was surprising, though.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.930
I had no idea Koga-senpai was 
such an incredible rider.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:39.280
He was the team's hope as a first-year.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.530
He couldn't ride for a long 
time due to an injury.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:48.950
Because he wanted to stay involved with 
the team, he'd been working as a mechanic.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:53.290
Huh? About the Inter-High...

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:56.670
Yeah, I'm not going. I'm staying here.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.970
Everyone's bikes are in perfect condition.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:03.080
What? But, uh...

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.970
It's just a stupid superstition, 
but if I'm around...

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.000
I have a feeling things will turn 
out like they did last year.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:11.980
What?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.100
It's fine.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:15.560
Don't worry about me. Good luck.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:18.480
I'm counting on you, first-years.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.410
Imaizumi, Naruko, Onoda...

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.900
Help Kinjou-san and the others win.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:28.330
That was painful for Koga-senpai.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.410
Teshima-san fights knowing all that.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.670
The same goes for Sugimoto.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:41.800
We carry the hopes of those who have fallen 
and can't participate in the Inter-High.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:47.360
Four days from now, either Teshima-san 
or Koga-san will carry those hopes.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:54.250
Then we have to get stronger 
during these four days.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.310
Yeah.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:12.710
That was rough, but I endured it.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.860
What do you think, Koga?

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:19.070
Tomorrow will be harder.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.220
Seriously?

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.840
And give me a hand. Hey, Koga!

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:29.850
<b>Teshima
 Koga
 Aoyagi
 Imaizumi</b>

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.400
I can't stand up.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.150
<i>I've waited a long time.</i>

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:39.400
<i>This year, I'll complete 
one thousand kilometers.</i>

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:43.900
<i>And fight at the Inter-High.</i>

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:47.300
Your pace is dropping with each lap.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.800
Are you okay, Junta?

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:53.790
Koga's a genius. I don't 
stand a chance against him.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:55.950
Junta...

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.250
That's why I'm thinking of doing...

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.580
...what only an ordinary man can do.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.280
<b>Boom</b>

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.510
<b>Pop</b>

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:11.840
Supersonic Oxygen Ten Thousand Bites of Food!

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:15.000
A man eats plain white rice in silence!

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.120
Aoyagi-san and Naruko-san are amazing!

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.670
They sure do eat a lot.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:27.430
<i>That's a lot of calories, though.</i>

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:30.610
<i>Bicycle racing is a battle of endurance.</i>

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:35.990
<i>Koga-senpai is putting it on the line 
in his race against Teshima-san.</i>

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.490
The skies cleared up, though.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:41.930
The fog was crazy this morning. Right, Onoda?

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:43.000
Yes, sir.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:48.010
We went for a ride first thing this morning

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:50.630
to make up for being late 
to the training camp.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:54.010
<b>Teshima
 Koga</b>

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:54.010
Now I'm back to being five 
minutes behind Teshima.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:59.030
Envision your assignment 
and goal while you ride.

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:00.100
Yes, sir!

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.710
Help provide food and water 
if you've dropped out.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.680
If you're free, work out.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:08.240
Yes, sir!

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:10.500
I'm off.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:20.830
What's this? I thought 
I'd gotten ahead of you.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.330
This is pointless. Choose.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:27.160
Will you push yourself today and 
drop out because of an injury,

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.880
or keep riding and drop out 
when you're exhausted tomorrow?

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.220
Sorry, but I choose the third option!

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.310
I'll complete a thousand 
kilometers in four days...

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.940
...and cross the finish line before you!

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:50.260
You may be a skilled strategist, 
but you're not good enough.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:51.570
Give up, Teshima.

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:54.570
<i>He's a hair's breadth away.</i>

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:57.910
<i>Only a genius could do something so easily.</i>

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.510
<i>In contrast, I'm ordinary.</i>

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:03.710
<i>I haven't even won a single race.</i>

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:15.300
<i>But Koga, there are sights 
that only I can see.</i>

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:21.060
<i>There's a lot to learn
from seeing him up close.</i>

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:23.950
What are you smiling about, Teshima?

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:25.770
Are you approaching your limit?

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:29.930
Koga!

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:31.440
I'm an ordinary man!

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:35.860
That's why I'll take one step at a time,
and during this training camp...

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.870
Become everything you said I'm not.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:43.820
Looks like you'll have to learn 
your lesson the hard way.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.750
You've always got to have the last word.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.750
I'll shut you up!

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:53.300
<i>The hard way? I know how strong you are.</i>

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.970
<i>I've always known.</i>

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:02.470
<i>During the Hiroshima Inter-High two years ago,
 at the end of the second day...</i>

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:06.980
<i>I can still recall that atmosphere.</i>

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:11.890
<i>That tense atmosphere of total despair.</i>

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:14.970
It's warped.

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:16.150
That's enough, Koga.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.780
But Kinjou-san asked me to fix it!

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:23.160
We only have one ace, and our mechanic 
doubles as one of our riders.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:28.630
It was wrong for a team as weak 
as ours to dream of winning.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.510
I'll fix it!

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:32.750
We're saying you don't have to!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.940
Sohoku High School's second-year ace, Kinjou,

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:40.430
is dropping out on the second 
day after a hard fall.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.020
Excuse me.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:47.730
Kinjou-san's being examined at the hospital.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:51.660
His has broken ribs, 
and abrasions in seven places.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:54.510
One of the third-years is 
going to stay with him.

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:57.110
I see.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:06.960
Tadokoro-san, tomorrow I'll be—

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.250
Get changed. You've done enough.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.460
Get some rest.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:15.090
We still have to race tomorrow.

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.430
The ace?

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.680
Keep your voice down, Junta.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.680
The ace, though? Are you serious?

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.860
Kinjou-san's done a lot for me.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:30.650
That's why I have to fill his spot.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:35.690
They won't be looking out for the first-years.
I'll be free to do as I please.

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:40.530
I'll sneak my way to the top 
just before the finish line tomorrow.

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:43.490
I'm confident in my sprinting ability,
so I'm going to go for it.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.860
If things go well, we could win.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.310
It'll be a huge comeback.
We'll get single-digit number tags.

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:50.330
Don't, Kimitaka.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.440
I understand how you feel.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:57.120
I dropped out of the thousand kilometer 
training camp, so you might not like me saying it,

00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:59.420
but you can't do it.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:01.770
Listen to the upperclassmen tomorrow.

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:02.390
Junta!

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.490
I thought you'd understand!

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:06.970
You're injured!

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:10.250
Kinjou-san said you didn't 
have to push yourself.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:14.460
He told you to ride in the Inter-High, 
get experience, and use it next year.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:15.860
What about this year?

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:20.860
He told you not to push yourself because 
you're talented and have promise!

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.980
It was the same during the training camp.

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:26.910
You started hurting on the fourth day,
so you were told to stop at 900 kilometers.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:30.250
But you injured yourself further by 
pushing yourself eighty kilometers more.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.580
You still haven't been able to get over that!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.380
I've healed. There's nothing to worry about.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.310
I recover quickly.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:39.210
Kimitaka...

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.550
You know my nickname, don't you?

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.520
I'm the iron man,

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:45.930
the Stamina Simpleton.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.260
Sohoku High School's first-year jumped ahead!

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.320
<i>I'm the team's hope.</i>

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:04.980
Your body is made for cycling.

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:06.830
If you keep at it, you'll get better.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.330
<i>They expect great things for me.</i>

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.560
<i>Kinjou-san's hopes...</i>

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.540
<i>I'll...</i>

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.250
There's a sharp turn at 
the bottom of the hill!

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.470
<i>I have to do well.</i>

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:28.050
<i>I have to do...</i>

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:31.730
Someone fell!

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:32.810
Are you okay?

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:39.330
Teshima...

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:41.350
Kimitaka...

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:43.880
<i>Number 73 has dropped out of the race.</i>

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:46.160
<i>He seems to have hit his left shoulder hard.</i>

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.670
They took him away.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:53.250
<b>Koga 73</b>

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.860
<i>Should I have done more to stop him?</i>

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:57.810
<i>Damn it. Why, Kimitaka?</i>

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:03.090
It's nighttime now, Koga.

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:06.090
No, Kimitaka.

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:10.360
They'll be putting out the no passing 
board by the finish line soon,

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:14.390
so we don't push ourselves too hard 
at night and injure ourselves.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:18.730
<i>Why? Nothing I did let me pull ahead of you.</i>

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.900
<i>You, an ordinary man.</i>

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:25.060
Kimitaka... That brings back memories.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:27.820
I used to call you that 
when we were still friends.

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:32.580
After your fall, as you were 
stoically blaming yourself,

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:35.870
I couldn't say anything to you.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:42.210
I'm glad you returned to this training 
camp so we could speak our minds.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:48.470
I believe there's a moment when 
an ordinary man beats a genius.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.220
Want to give it a try?

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:56.230
Let's race to the finish line 
where the no passing sign is.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:01.360
Can I assume this race 
will settle everything,

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:02.760
Junta!

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:06.400
Yeah, that's right.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:08.360
Kimitaka!

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.450
A-Aoyagi-san!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.120
Are you taking a break?

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:25.280
You guys should watch this, too.

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:29.380
Is this the end of their race?

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.030
Teshima-san and Koga-senpai are...

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:37.390
They probably intend to decide 
who will ride in the Inter-High.

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:41.880
<i>Teshima-san has responded to all of 
Koga-senpai's movements</i>

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:43.940
<i>and persistently kept up.</i>

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:48.360
<b>Teshima
 Koga
 Aoyagi
 Imaizumi</b>

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:48.360
<i>We thought he was at a disadvantage,
but he's still just barely keeping even.</i>

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:54.140
<i>Is Teshima-san pushing and testing 
himself to find his answer?</i>

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:56.770
<i>Junta...</i>

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:01.170
Sorry for winning again, Teshima.

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.510
It's fine. I'm satisfied.

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:07.150
We beat the elites together.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:10.220
You're the one who deserves 
to be first, Teshima.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:12.530
I'll assist you in the next race.

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.600
Don't you know?

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:19.480
I've never won a sprint to the finish before.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:21.940
Teshima!

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:25.370
I struggled hard, but it was no use.

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:26.810
I'm 11th.

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:29.630
One shy of the top ten.

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:30.490
Sounds like me, right?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.150
Even after you pulled for me.

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:35.160
Sorry.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:42.330
My race with Koga will probably end 
either tomorrow or the day after.

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:45.340
In my exhausted state, I have 
to beat the genius Koga

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:50.170
in a finish line sprint,
which I've never won before.

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:51.560
<i>Junta...</i>

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.510
If it comes down to it, Aoyagi...

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:59.600
Will you cheer for me?

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:03.180
<i>I'm at my limit.</i>

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:07.230
<i>I'm amazed my legs are still pedaling.</i>

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:10.280
<i>But I won't give up.</i>

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:17.740
<i>Why can't an ordinary man with ordinary legs 
miraculously beat a genius just once?</i>

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:20.470
They're close. I see two lights.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.710
Will you cheer for me?

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:28.780
<i>Of course. Who else would I be cheering for?</i>

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:30.420
Junta!

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:32.960
Is Koga-senpai riding alone?

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:35.930
No, Teshima-san is right behind him.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:41.470
Teshima-san is avoiding the wind by staying behind,
 but he looks like he's struggling.

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.230
<i>Junta...</i>

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:46.730
Koga will go all out at the training camp.

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:50.120
I probably won't have time to be the captain.

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:53.930
Could you lead the team for me, then?

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.240
I understand. I'm the vice-captain.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.460
I don't want to have any regrets.

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:07.500
If I fail, this will be the last time.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:12.510
<i>I'm uncertain about facing 
the Inter-High without you.</i>

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:18.840
<i>Keep moving. Don't stop.</i>

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:21.670
<i>Do what you've never done before.</i>

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:26.310
<i>You still had that much strength left, Junta?</i>

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:30.070
<i>I'm going to the Inter-High!</i>

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:32.780
They're neck and neck!

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.400
Teshima-san's pulling ahead!

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:38.660
I've never seen Teshima-san so strong before.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.120
He's going to make it.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.200
Did you notice, hotshot?

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:45.040
Naruko...

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.710
Since the sprint started, 
Koga-senpai hasn't...

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:50.960
...stood up from his saddle once.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:55.470
<i>One hundred and fifty meters left.
That's enough.</i>

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:00.050
Koga-senpai...

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:01.390
Stood up!

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:10.560
<i>I'll do it.</i>

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:15.570
<i>What's wrong, guys? I can't hear you.</i>

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:18.840
<i>No one's crossed the finish line yet.</i>

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:21.370
<i>I guess it can't be helped.</i>

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:24.140
<i>It's always been this way.</i>

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:28.660
<i>No one's ever expected anything from me.</i>

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:31.310
Class 1-5, Teshima Junta.

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:32.150
Yes, sir.

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:33.710
You're skinny.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:36.450
Your jersey looks new. Are you a beginner?

00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:40.500
Ah... I rode in middle school.

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:43.720
I thought I could turn over 
a new leaf with this jersey.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.480
You're Koga, huh?

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:46.720
We've heard about you.

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:53.480
This training camp is hard. Do your best.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:58.360
Kinjou, Tadokoro, Makishima, and first-year Koga,
 finish your thousand kilometers.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:01.480
Teshima, ride as hard as you can.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.910
Huh? Yes, sir.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:05.410
<i>"As hard as I can?"</i>

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:09.370
<i>He doesn't expect a thousand 
kilometers from me.</i>

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:14.250
I'm the one who trained Teshima and Aoyagi.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.510
<i>Tadokoro-san's the only 
one who believed in me.</i>

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:23.760
That's enough, Teshima, Aoyagi.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:26.980
<i>I couldn't meet his expectations.</i>

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:30.390
<i>But I understand now.</i>

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:35.570
<i>I was jealous of how everyone 
expected so much from Koga.</i>

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:40.160
<i>I thought I could work harder if 
they had high expectations for me.</i>

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:43.530
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:47.450
<i>It should've been obvious once
I thought about it. That's right.</i>

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:50.370
<i>Unless I work hard,
no one will expect anything.</i>

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:55.520
<i>Can I do something I've never done before now?</i>

00:19:55.990 --> 00:20:00.860
<i>I can. There's one man standing 
over there who believes in me.</i>

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:03.340
Junta, win!

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:06.180
<i>I'll become stronger. I'll become stronger.</i>

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:08.400
<i>Because I'm weak.</i>

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:15.980
<i>This is it!</i>

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:22.450
<i>H-He's beside me?</i>

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.830
Junta!

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:33.370
<b>
 
 
Aoyagi</b>

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:34.620
<b>Teshima
 
Aoyagi</b>

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:35.250
<b>Teshima
Koga
Aoyagi</b>

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:38.840
Teshima-san won the race!

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:49.560
I... lost? I lost a sprint?

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:56.110
<i>When I passed him at the end,
I didn't think he'd pass me back.</i>

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:01.440
I believe there's a moment when 
an ordinary man beats a genius.

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:06.320
Crap. I'm at my limit.

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:10.160
An ordinary man beats a genius...

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:13.140
Kimitaka!

00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:17.960
That was close.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:22.070
I can't believe you wore me down so much.

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:25.470
Me, the Stamina Simpleton.

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:28.240
Thank you, Junta.

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:33.770
Your eyes are brimming with confidence.

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:37.980
Sohoku High School's fate is in your hands.

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:41.630
Go win, Junta.

00:23:17.710 --> 00:23:18.660
Junta...

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:29.950
Aoyagi, my hair's silky now, too.

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:31.300
Junta?

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:35.820
Junta...

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT RIDE  Koga's Goal</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
